body:
@dalexeev 

Pushed an alternate solution that is more code, but employs the Enum Scope Searching already used by _get_property_help_data (which was behaving correctly even before this PR) and performs the same search in _get_constant_help_data

Does not change any of the DocData generation

I realize the new method works much better, but there is still an Ambiguity problem.

```
else if (dot_pos >= 0) {
		String enum_class_name = String(p_class_name).left(dot_pos);
		String enum_name = String(p_class_name).substr(dot_pos + 1);
		const DocData::ClassDoc *enum_class = EditorHelp::get_doc(enum_class_name);
		if (enum_class) {
			// Non-native constants shouldn't be cached, nor translated.
			const bool is_native = !enum_class->is_script_doc;

			for (DocData::ConstantDoc constant : enum_class->constants) {
				HelpData current;
				current.description = HANDLE_DOC(constant.description);

				if (constant.name == p_constant_name && constant.enumeration == enum_name) {
					result = current;

					if (!is_native) {
						break;
					}
				}

				if (is_native) {
					doc_constant_cache[p_class_name][constant.name] = current;
				}
			}
		}
	}
```

This method will always correctly grab Docstring values from NamedEnums, but will fail to grab the DocString from an unnamed enum if there is also a named enum with the same value name.

```
enum Blah {
	A = 0, ## You fool, this is the wrong one
	B = 1, ## ALSO INCORRECT
}

enum {
	A = 0, ## DocComment
	B = 1, ## DocComment
}

var something = self.A # shows the tooltip for Blah.A
```

Is there any issue with assigning a generic, constant, prefix to either Value groups ConstDoc names to ensure that duplicate names across distinct enums remain unique?

So instead of `{"A": You fool..., "B": Also, "A": DocComment, "B": DocComment}`

Generate ConstDocNames such that we have `{"EnumA": You fool..., "EnumB": Also, "A": DocComment, "B": DocComment}`

Two named Enums with identical value names can still be differentiated by the ` && constant.enumeration == enum_name` clause, but the prefix would exist to differentiate Constants from NamedEnums and Constants from UnnamedEnums that get saved directly as class constants.
